<h2>Common Claim Issues and Insurer Arguments</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Splitting causes.</strong> The insurer accepts the roof damage but denies interior water as &ldquo;long-term leakage&rdquo; or &ldquo;no storm-created opening.&rdquo;</li>
<li><strong>Flood vs. wind-driven rain.</strong> Water at floor level is attributed to excluded surface water.</li>
<li><strong>Multiple storms.</strong> With several storm days in a single season, the carrier may argue part of the damage came from an earlier date or a prior claim.</li>
<li><strong>Incomplete interior scope.</strong> Drying, insulation, paint, and flooring continuity are underestimated.</li>
<li><strong>Mold.</strong> Delayed drying leads to mold, which many policies limit or exclude.</li>
</ul>
